    "html": "<p>Specific energy and energy density are used to characterize the energy content of various fuels. The table provides data for four different liquid fuels.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th></th><th>Specific energy / <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\text{MJ kg}^{-1}\"></span></th><th>Energy density / <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\text{GJ m}^{-3}\"></span></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr data-label=\"A\"><td>A.</td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"40\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"28\"></span></td></tr><tr data-label=\"B\"><td>B.</td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"20\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"18\"></span></td></tr><tr data-label=\"C\"><td>C.</td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"30\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"24\"></span></td></tr><tr data-label=\"D\"><td>D.</td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"50\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"40\"></span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Which fuel has the highest mass density?</p>"
